urces could be retrieved in this run.","unit":"CD2009-seke-banza","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"}]}],"sources":{},"units":{"CD2009-seke-banza":"Seke-Banza territory (Kongo-Central, between Matadi and Boma north of the Congo river) contains Seke-Banza centre, the Kitsiengo/Mbenza Thubi agglomeration, the Inga hydroelectric site and rural villages of the Seke-Banza and Inga health zones. No armed group holds territory here; the area is far from the eastern conflict zones. Towns are policed by the PNC with territorial administration and customary chiefs handling disputes; the Inga dam complex is a strategic site with additional FARDC/state security deployment. Past Bundu dia Kongo (BDK/BDM) political unrest in Kongo-Central did not displace state control. Web search was unavailable in this run (search budget exhausted), so the assessment rests on default state presence."}}